{
  "assembly_notes": "Root is support_frame; the seat is its PRISMATIC +Z child (seat_lift) and every height_mechanism candidate adds its rotary control(s) as REVOLUTE children of the frame, so the model carries at least two movable joints in every reachable configuration -- height adjustment is the category's core mechanism, not an option. storage=hinged_lid_box adds a third (the -X rear-edge lid hinge) and turns the lid into the seating surface. There are no compatibility gates: seat_form publishes one plan profile (rectangular extent or radius) that drives the frame-top ring/ledge, the storage box and lid outline, and the mechanism mount span, so a round seat on a four-leg frame with a storage box builds a round top ring, a round box and a round lid rather than being excluded.",
